      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ :\n\"قَضَى عَلِيٌّ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ فِي رَجُلٍ تَزَوَّجَ اِمْرَأَةَ رَجُلٍ أَنَّهُ رَجَمَ اَلْمَرْأَةَ وَ ضَرَبَ اَلرَّجُلَ اَلْحَدَّ وَ قَالَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ \"لَوْ عَلِمْتُ أَنَّكَ عَلِمْتَ لَفَضَخْتُ رَأْسَكَ بِالْحِجَارَةِ\" \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4994 - Shuayb narrated from Abu Baṣir who said that Abu Jafar (as) said:\n\"Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (as) ruled in the case of a man who married another man's wife, that the woman should be stoned, and the man should be given the prescribed punishment (for fornication).\nImam (as) then said: 'If I knew that you were aware (that she was already married), I would have crushed your head with stones.'\""
        ]
      }
